  "id": "BIT-ghost-2026-105647",
  "summary": "Ghost: Server-Side Request Forgery in Bookmark Fetching",
  "details": "Ghost is a Node.js content management system. From 6.54.1 until 6.65.0, a validation issue allowed some functionality, such as Webmentions, to be abused by an unauthenticated user to make limited HTTP requests to hosts in the Ghost server's internal network. A successful attack would not result in any response data being returned. This issue is fixed in version 6.65.0.",
